","ends":"2026-10-27T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8941c78c56646c68845dc0df12019ecf6fd1ddb5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8941c78c56646c68845dc0df12019ecf6fd1ddb5.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 25 at 8:05AM MDT until October 26 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Sunday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-26T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1709e90ff1e34c7424f08775fbd1301e1f7eb6e1.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1709e90ff1e34c7424f08775fbd1301e1f7eb6e1.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-25T11:31:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 251131 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 531 AM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026 .KEY ME